{"name":"Lemon Delicious","hex":"#fce699","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"lemon","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A yellowish citrus fruit.","A semitropical evergreen tree, Citrus limon, that bears such fruits."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Containing or having the flavour/flavor and/or scent of lemons.","Of the pale yellow colour/color of lemons."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/lemon"},{"term":"delicious","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Pleasing to the sense of taste; tasty.","Pleasing to a person's taste; pleasing to the eyes or mind."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/delicious"}],"entries":[{"title":"Lemon","blocks":[{"text":"The lemon is a species of small evergreen tree in the Citrus genus of the flowering plant family Rutaceae. A true lemon is a hybrid of the citron and the bitter orange. Its origins are uncertain, but some evidence suggests lemons originated during the 1st millennium BC in what is now northeastern India. Some other citrus fruits are called lemon."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/P1030323.JPG/330px-P1030323.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon","wikidata":"Q500"},{"title":"Lemon (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Lemon or lemon-color is a vivid yellow color characteristic of the lemon fruit. Shades of \"lemon\" may vary significantly from the fruit's actual color, including fluorescent tones and creamy hues reflective of lemon pies and confections."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f7/Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg/330px-Lemon_-_whole_and_split.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lemon_(color)","wikidata":"Q2720565"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3f/Lemon-citrus_limon_seedling.jpg/250px-Lemo